<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2015-girardia-17--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2015-girardia-17: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.32";
    dc:description "Direction of an instructive signal from soma to stem cells is a perturbation claim with a shape and stem-cell readout. PlanMine covers planarian gene expression and does not contain this signalling interruption. The proposal stays dependent on new cell-type-resolved experiments.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Interrupt candidate gap-junction-dependent signals from differentiated tissue to neoblasts or their progeny during regeneration and measure whether new tissue shape and neoblast position change while neoblast-intrinsic programs are held fixed. Loss of directed shaping only when that soma-to-neoblast path is blocked would support the proposal.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "No public dataset pairs a targeted somatic gap-junction block with neoblast position and final head shape.", "The instructive signal's molecular identity is left open, so several blocks could be counted as tests.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.62"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.319"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "needs-new-data".
